        <briefdescription>
<para>Performs the forward pass of this fully connected layer. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Computes the affine transformation Y = XW + b by first performing matrix multiplication of the input tensor with the weight matrix, then broadcasting the bias vector along a new first dimension to match the batch size of the input, and finally adding the broadcast bias to the weighted output elementwise. Each of these operations participates in the computational graph, allowing gradients to be propagated back through this layer during backpropagation.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>inputTensor</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The input tensor of shape (batchSize x inputs) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>A <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1TensorView" kindref="compound">TensorView</ref> containing the output of shape (batchSize x outputs) </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
